ros-humble-vda5050-connector (2.0.0-1jammy) jammy; urgency=high

  * First release for ROS 2 Humble.
    (#31 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/31>,
    #33 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/33>)
  * **Breaking:** order rejections now report ``errorType: "validationError"``
    (VDA 5050 §6.6.4.1) instead of the non-standard ``"validationOrder"``.
    Anything that matches on the old string needs updating.
    (#83 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/83>)
  * **Breaking:** with VDA 5050 2.x, the ``state`` message now carries
    ``information``, the 2.x field name, instead of the 1.x ``informations``.
    The ROS 2 ``OrderState`` message keeps ``informations``; 1.x is unchanged.
    (#43 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/43>)
  * New ``known_map_ids`` parameter: when set, orders whose nodes reference
    any other ``mapId`` are rejected with ``validationError``.
    (#83 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/83>)
  * New ``vda5050_protocol_version`` parameter for the MQTT bridge; topics use
    its major version. (#53 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/53>)
  * New ``enable_nav_through_nodes`` mode: the controller sends the adapter one
    ``NavigateThroughNodes`` goal for several nodes and extends it with
    ``ExtendNavigation`` as the order grows, stopping at nodes with blocking actions.
    (#75 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/75>,
    #80 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/80>,
    #86 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/86>)
  * Malformed orders are rejected with ``validationError`` instead of being
    dropped, and a malformed MQTT message no longer stops the bridge.
    (#84 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/84>,
    #94 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/94>)
  * Orders whose ``nodePosition`` has no ``theta`` are accepted (optional in
    VDA 5050 2.x); the adapter gets NaN.
    (#93 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/93>)
  * Serial numbers that aren't valid ROS 2 names (e.g. ``0001``) work; MQTT topics
    keep them unchanged. (#92 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/92>)
  * ``interface_name`` can be configured, and the operating mode comes from the
    adapter's state. (#60 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/60>)
  * ``errorReferences`` keys are camelCase.
    (#72 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/72>)
  * Order handling fixes: stitching uses the last node of the base, action states
    survive stitching, failed navigation goals and failed actions are reported,
    a canceled order's errors are cleared, and instant actions don't count as an
    active order.
    (#42 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/42>,
    #45 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/45>,
    #60 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/60>,
    #64 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/64>,
    #65 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/65>,
    #68 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/68>,
    #69 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/69>,
    #76 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/76>)
  * Edge trajectory control points keep their orientation.
    (#63 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/63>)
  * MQTT bridge: retries until the first broker connection succeeds, exits cleanly
    on SIGINT, and logs connection errors without raising.
    (#55 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/55>,
    #70 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/70>,
    #73 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/73>,
    #85 <https://github.com/inorbit-ai/ros_amr_interop/issues/85>)

 -- "Leandro Pineda" <leandro@inorbit.ai>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0000

